const privacy = `<section class="hero page-hero container"><h1>Website privacy.</h1><p class="hero-subtitle">Choose whether to share analytics.</p></section><section class="container section privacy-copy"><h2>Optional website analytics</h2><p>With your permission, this website uses Google Analytics to measure page visits, approximate visitor counts, referrals, and clicks on Wixal release downloads. Google receives browser and device information and processes your IP address. Analytics cookies distinguish browsers; these counts do not identify individual people.</p><p>Google Analytics loads only after you choose Allow analytics. You can change your choice using Analytics preferences in the footer. Declining keeps website analytics off. Downloads and all site pages remain available.</p><h2>Download clicks and GitHub downloads</h2><p>A download click records a request to open a release file. It does not prove a completed download or an installation. GitHub independently counts downloads of release assets, including direct links outside this site and repeated downloads.</p><h2>Public visitor total</h2><p>The site publishes only the aggregate active-user count for the last 30 days and the report update time. This count covers visitors who allow analytics and can be affected by browser blocking and Google processing delays. It updates daily.</p><h2>Your desktop workspace</h2><p>This website integration does not add telemetry to the Wixal app or send your projects, prompts, chats, model output, or notes to Google Analytics.</p><p><a class="inline-link" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a> · <a class="inline-link" href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a></p></section>`;
